    <statement><p>A potter forms a piece of clay into a right circular cylinder. 
As she rolls it, the height <m>h</m> of the cylinder 
increases and the radius <m>r</m> decreases.  Assume that 
no clay is lost in the process.  Suppose the height of 
the cylinder is increasing by <m>0.4</m> centimeters 
per second.  What is the rate at which the radius is 
changing when the radius is <m>6</m> centimeters and the 
height is <m>10</m> centimeters?</p>
<p><fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0001"/>
(Include  with your
answer.)</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-0.12\ {\textstyle\frac{\rm\mathstrut cm}{\rm\mathstrut s}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
